                <pb facs="0539" n="419" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg419"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">813.00 Tacoma/–: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Ramer</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-08-03T09:00:00-05:45"><hi rendition="#italic">August 3,
                                1922—9 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 3:25 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>40. Morales’ 61, August 1, 2 p.m. to the Department. Nicaraguan Government agrees
                    to Gulf of Fonseca as meeting place for conference and is ready to go at the
                    Department’s convenience. I suggest that the <hi rendition="#italic">Tacoma</hi>
                    call first at Corinto for Nicaraguan delegation.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ramer</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
